  "question": {
    "text": "<p>In the reported figure, two bodies <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>and</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;of masses <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>200</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>800</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> are attached with the system of springs. Springs are kept in a stretched position with some extension when the system is released. The horizontal surface is assumed to be frictionless. The angular frequency will be _______&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>rad</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> when <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><msup><mn>1</mn><mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></msup></math>.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/ffad789d-7c67-44a7-8ddd-a2eb504f2fc7-image.png\" style=\"width: 338px; height: 82px;\" /></p>",
    "image": null
